  "method": {
    "input": "Previously reviewed original-PyTorch CPU forward/backward masks; no model inference or source video decoding.",
    "rules": {
      "higherObjectScore": "Take the direction with higher raw presence logit; both-empty and seed have no selection.",
      "largerMask": "Take the direction with more foreground pixels; ties explicit.",
      "smallerNonemptyMask": "Among nonempty masks choose fewer foreground pixels; if just one is nonempty use it."
    },
    "queue": "IoU below 0.90 for nonempty union, plus first/last two frames of each shared-empty interval. Thresholds 0.50/0.75/0.90/0.95 reported for review sensitivity, not fitted acceptance gates.",
    "qualitativeEvidence": "Thirteen selected cases from prior visual review; frames224 and343 additionally viewed full size in this turn. Relative preference is not perfect-mask ground truth. No headline accuracy percentage.",
    "seed": "Frame375 excluded from rule comparison and queue; its backward score is forced and mask is identical by construction."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Higher raw score selects a known wrong mask at224 (wrong foreground hand in backward) and343 (wrong foreground hand in forward). It favors the useful direction in many other reviewed cases, but cannot be adopted as an identity decision.",
    "Larger masks include wrong foreground at224/225/229/346/354/360. Smaller-nonempty chooses the less useful forward mask at277 and still selects the wrong lone foreground hand at343.",
    "Both directions miss the visible target sliver310. Score/area selection and overlap cannot recover a mask neither direction produced. This case is brought into view by shared-absence boundary inspection, not solved.",
    "At IoU0.90,105 frames form8 disagreement intervals. Adding12 shared-absence boundary frames queues117 of210 nonseed frames. This is a large review burden, not a demonstrated automatic-efficiency improvement.",
    "Sensitivity queues95/101/105/111 disagreement frames at IoU0.50/0.75/0.90/0.95. The0.50 queue misses the wrong-hand224..226 disagreement (IoU about0.61..0.65). No cutoff is validated.",
    "Unflagged high-overlap masks or shared-empty interiors remain unverified; queue membership is not a label. No generalization claim beyond this development clip."
  ],
